            {
              "id": "bf3d52f4-c21b-4a09-b353-e55853769604",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Shared Fantasy: Role Playing Games As Social Worlds</strong></em> was written by Gary Alan Fine, published by University of Chicago Press, December 1, 1983."
            },
            {
              "id": "38fb1be8-64e3-4fa2-8b20-77fbc9a84196",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1110ae15-28cd-458b-ac95-7ea2bfe2d6d7",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>This classic study still provides one of the most acute descriptions available of an often misunderstood subculture: that of fantasy role playing games like </em>Dungeons &amp; Dragons<em>. Gary Alan Fine immerses himself in several different gaming systems, offering insightful details on the nature of the games and the patterns of interaction among players,as well as their reasons for playing.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "d8b697a2-e5c9-4c0b-b1e3-e4bfc2f8965b",
              "type": "paragraph",
